{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/920771-hack-switching-around-the-mechanics-for-analysts-and-psychopomps-thoughts","id":920771,"title":"[Hack] Switching around the mechanics for Analysts and Psychopomps - thoughts?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-24T21:26:22-07:00","id":920771,"title":"[Hack] Switching around the mechanics for Analysts and Psychopomps - thoughts?","content":"It kinda throws me that Analysts, the extremely unobtrusive Incarnation, has major mechanical incentives based entirely around Exploits. Now, that's because they were added after-the-fact to Demon, but I'm still contemplating taking the emphasis on Mundane Embeds from Psychopomps and giving them to Analysts, which not only fits Analysts but has never really felt like something that screams &quot;Psychopomps&quot; to me. Now granted, Exploits really aren't their bag either, but I still might be more comfortable with this arrangement.<br /> <br /> Do you guys have any thoughts on the matter?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage the Awakening 2e Communal Homebrew Threads:<br /> - <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/966394-perils-of-the-path-post-your-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Perils of the Path</a> - Other homebrew threads linked in the OP!<br /> <br /> Join us at the unofficial IRC channels on.irc.sorcery.net at #exalted and now #theonyxpath!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/451-kirby-jerusalem","name":"Kirby Jerusalem","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar451_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"589"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-24T22:11:10-07:00","id":920793,"title":"","content":"I feel that conflating &quot;Mundane Embeds are where most stealth-oriented demon tricks are&quot; with &quot;Analysts are a class of Incarnation largely kept secret by the God-Machine&quot; (which seems to be the logic here) is a poor fit.<br /> <br /> Wheels get Mundane Embeds for the Cover-management and materiel/personnel effects, which serve as an extension of their jobs to ensure things are in the right place when the time comes. Finding lost items, disposing of evidence, making sure everyone's stories line up, getting access to privileged locations? These are things that fixers and builders and transporters need to be able to do. Psychopomps are the demons that are best-equipped to hide from the Machine within Its own systems.<br /> <br /> Analysts, meanwhile, were as close as the God-Machine got to directly devoting angelic processing power to research and development. Running tests and extrapolating conclusions from available data are part of the thematic basis for their faculty with Exploits in a way that fails to be as central if they're simply given an affinity for the class of Embeds least useful in a last stand. It makes sense that the demons most directly associated with the Machine's closely-guarded experimentation do naturally best at applying Godly principles to the fringes of those occult shortcuts' designed purposes.<br /> <br /> I could definitely see a case to be made for changing which Incarnation was the &quot;extra&quot; one, but the knock-on effects of swapping construction and scrutiny in the God-Machine's prioritization of Infrastructure-secrecy probably bear consideration despite the greater ease with which one can assign best-fit Agendas to Incarnations.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":111,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","user":"Satchel","date":". 06-25-2016, 01:29 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}